## Kagaz Additional Terms

### Using Kagaz

You may install and use the software, unchanged, for any purpose,
personal or at work, free of charge, if you got it from an official
source: a release published by the licensor, or the official
repository. This is in addition to the permitted purposes of the
PolyForm Strict License 1.0.0.

### Building it yourself

You may download the source code from the official repository and
build it without changes, for your own use or your organization's own
internal use. A build you make is only for that use: you may not give
it to anyone else.

### Contributing

You may make changes to the software only to prepare a contribution
to the official repository. You may share those changes only by
submitting them to the official repository (a pull request, say),
under the Kagaz Contributor License Agreement (CLA.md in the official
repository). A fork kept on GitHub for that purpose is allowed. You
may not use your changes for anything else.

### Not allowed without the licensor's written permission

1. Distributing the software or any build of it, changed or not:
   publishing, sharing, mirroring, uploading it to an app store,
   selling, renting or lending it. Pointing people to an official
   source is fine.
2. Making changes, forks or other works based on the software, other
   than contributions as above.
3. Copying the source code, or any substantial part of it, into other
   software.
4. Translating or porting the software, or any substantial part of its
   source code, into another programming language, or rewriting it by
   working from its source code; and publishing any such work, under
   any license.
5. Giving the source code, or any substantial part of it, to an AI
   system (a coding agent, an AI assistant or chatbot, or any other
   machine-learning model) to have it write software that does what
   Kagaz does, or that copies its design, structure or code, in any
   programming language. What the AI system writes counts as a work
   based on the software, even when it writes it from scratch, and
   item 4 applies to it. Using an AI system to read, explain or check
   the code, or to prepare a contribution under "Contributing", is
   allowed.
6. Using the source code, or any part of it, to train, fine-tune or
   evaluate an AI system, or including it in a dataset made for that,
   whether the AI system is for your own use, shared or sold.
7. Making money from the software: selling it or any work based on it,
   charging for it or for access to it, offering it as a paid service,
   or bundling it with anything sold. Using the official software,
   unchanged, in your own work is not making money from it.
8. Removing or changing this license, the Required Notice, or the
   licensor's other notices.

### Asking for permission

For anything these terms do not allow, ask the licensor by opening an
issue in the official repository. Permission counts only when given
in writing.

### Other people's components

Kagaz uses libraries made by others, under their own licenses. These
terms do not change those licenses, and do not take away any right
those licenses give you to those components.

